-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lance file format
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nanolance is an independent C++ implementation of the Lance columnar file format.
It does NOT link the Lance reference implementation (the Rust `lance` crate); it
writes/reads the format directly. However, its protobuf message definitions —
manifests, data files, column/page metadata, and encodings — are derived from the
Lance project's `.proto` schemas, pinned at tag v7.0.0-rc.1:

    Lance — https://github.com/lance-format/lance
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The generated protobuf code (generated/lance_minimal.pb.*) and the proto pin notes
(third_party/lance_proto/) are based on those Apache-2.0 definitions.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lance-c headers
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
compat/lance-c/include/lance/lance.h and lance.hpp are copied unmodified from the
lance-c project at the commit named in compat/lance-c/UPSTREAM, so that nanolance's
liblance_c (src/lance_c.cpp) offers exactly lance-c's C and C++ API:

    lance-c - https://github.com/lance-format/lance-c
    Copyright The Lance Authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    (compat/lance-c/LICENSE).

nanolance's implementation of that API is independent of lance-c's and is not
affiliated with the Lance project.

The pylance-compatible Python module (bindings/python/nanolance/lance) follows the
names and signatures of pylance's API (https://github.com/lance-format/lance,
Apache-2.0); its input coercion follows pylance's lance.types._coerce_reader.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other third-party software
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
These are pulled in at build time via CMake FetchContent (not redistributed here):

  - Apache Arrow nanoarrow  - Apache License 2.0  - https://github.com/apache/arrow-nanoarrow
  - Zstandard (zstd)        - BSD-3-Clause        - https://github.com/facebook/zstd
  - CLI11                   - BSD-3-Clause        - https://github.com/CLIUtils/CLI11

The built-in S3 reader (optional, -DNANOLANCE_ENABLE_S3=ON; off by default) additionally links these
system libraries dynamically (not redistributed here):

  - libcurl                 - curl license (MIT/X11-style)  - https://curl.se
  - OpenSSL (libcrypto)     - Apache License 2.0 (3.x)      - https://www.openssl.org

See THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md for details. The pcapng2lance example additionally
depends on the sister nanotins stack (Apache-2.0); see its own NOTICE.
